<PageLayout title="Privacy policy" lead="What data this site processes, and why. As of November 2026.">
  <p>
    This site is built to collect as little data as possible. It uses no cookies, no analytics or tracking tools and
    no advertising networks. Fonts are hosted on this site itself, and the calculators run entirely in your browser:
    the numbers you enter are never sent anywhere.
  </p>

  <h2>Controller</h2>
  <p>
    Julian Radkov<br />
    Leibnizstraße 110, 10625 Berlin, Germany<br />
    Email: <a href="mailto:julian.kolev@outlook.com">julian.kolev@outlook.com</a>
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting and delivery</h2>
  <p>
    This site is hosted and delivered by Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend St., San Francisco, CA 94107, USA. When you
    visit a page, your browser sends technical data to Cloudflare's servers, such as your IP address, the page
    requested, the time, your browser type and the referring page. Cloudflare needs this data to deliver the site and
    to protect it against attacks and abuse. For the parts of the site that run code on the server (the affiliate links
    and the contact form, described below), short-lived error and request logs are kept for a few days to find and fix
    faults.
  </p>
  <p>
    The legal basis is our legitimate interest in delivering a secure and working website (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
    Cloudflare processes the data on our behalf under a data processing agreement (Art. 28 GDPR). Data may be
    transferred to the USA. Cloudflare is certified under the EU-U.S. Data Privacy Framework, and the EU Standard
    Contractual Clauses also apply.
  </p>

  <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
  <p>
    Some links on this site are affiliate links (they start with <code>/go/</code>). When you click one, we count the
    click anonymously before forwarding you to the partner's website. We record only which link was clicked, on which
    page, the country (derived from the request, not stored as an address) and whether the device is mobile or
    desktop. We do not store your IP address and set no cookies. These counts are kept for up to three months and
    tell us which articles are useful. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in understanding which pages earn
    commission (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
  </p>
  <p>
    The partner learns that you came from this site and, as a reference code, which article you clicked on, so that
    it can credit us with a commission. Once you are on the partner's website, its own privacy policy applies,
    including any cookies it sets.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact form</h2>
  <p>
    If you use the contact form, we process your name, your email address and your message in order to answer you.
    The message is sent to our inbox by email through Brevo (Sendinblue SAS, 106 boulevard Haussmann, 75008 Paris,
    France), which acts on our behalf under a data processing agreement. The site itself does not store your message.
    We keep the email as long as needed to deal with your request and delete it afterwards, unless legal retention
    duties apply. The legal basis is your request (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR) and our legitimate interest in answering
    messages (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
  </p>
  <p>
    To keep spam and abuse out, the form uses two protections. Cloudflare Turnstile checks that you are a person, not a
    bot: when you open the contact page, it loads a script from Cloudflare and processes technical data such as your
    IP address and browser characteristics. And your IP address is used briefly to limit how many messages can be sent
    per minute; it is not stored. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in protecting the form from abuse
    (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR). Reading technical information from your device for this purpose is necessary to provide the
    contact form you asked to use (§ 25(2) no. 2 TDDDG).
  </p>
  <p>
    You can also write to us directly by email. We then process your email address and message for the same purpose
    and on the same legal basis.
  </p>

  <h2>Light and dark mode</h2>
  <p>
    If you switch between light and dark mode, your choice is saved in your browser's local storage, so the site
    remembers it on your next visit. This is not a cookie, it is not sent to us, and you can delete it at any time in
    your browser settings. Storing it is necessary to provide the function you asked for (§ 25(2) no. 2 TDDDG).
  </p>

  {/* Newsletter: once a newsletter provider is set up (site.newsletterAction), add a section here: provider name and
      address, data processing agreement, double opt-in, legal basis (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR), how to unsubscribe. */}

  <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>
    Articles link to sources such as laws, tax offices and insurers. Nothing is sent to those websites unless you
    click a link. Once you are there, their own privacy policies apply.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>You have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access the personal data we hold about you (Art. 15 GDPR),</li>
    <li>have incorrect data corrected (Art. 16 GDPR),</li>
    <li>have your data deleted (Art. 17 GDPR),</li>
    <li>have processing restricted (Art. 18 GDPR),</li>
    <li>receive your data in a portable format (Art. 20 GDPR),</li>
    <li>
      object to processing based on legitimate interest, for reasons arising from your particular situation
      (Art. 21 GDPR).
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>To use these rights, email us at the address above.</p>
  <p>
    You can also complain to a data protection supervisory authority. The authority responsible for us is the Berlin
    Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information (Berliner Beauftragte für Datenschutz und
    Informationsfreiheit), Alt-Moabit 59–61, 10555 Berlin.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We update this policy when the site changes, for example when a new service is added. The date at the top shows
    the current version.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
